        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buzzing, humming, clicking and a whirring fan are the normal soundtrack of induction cooking, and nearly all of it comes from the pan, the power level or the hob pacing itself at low settings. Heavier, flatter pans and lower settings quiet most of it down.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Crackling from the hob itself, burning smells, returning error codes and zones that cut out are different. Switch off, note the code and model number, and contact the manufacturer or an authorized technician rather than opening the unit yourself.
          </p>
